and as it gets narrower
I'm gonna do half circles

00:09:38.219 --> 00:09:39.680
to get wedges.

00:09:39.680 --> 00:09:41.430
My circles look good.

00:09:41.430 --> 00:09:43.730
I feel like we're gonna get a
lot of pasta out of this one.

00:09:43.730 --> 00:09:45.420
All right, let's do a
little bit of cleanup.

00:09:45.420 --> 00:09:47.620
We're gonna shave off the sides here.

00:09:47.620 --> 00:09:48.630
We got lemons!

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:50.570
It's time to fill them.

00:09:50.570 --> 00:09:52.690
We have so many raviolos today.

00:09:52.690 --> 00:09:53.820
Wait, no, these are ravioli.

00:09:53.820 --> 00:09:55.350
One is raviolo, right?

00:09:55.350 --> 00:09:56.183
No one knows.

00:09:56.183 --> 00:09:57.090
Please tell us the answers.

00:09:57.090 --> 00:10:00.480
5 plus 5 is 10, plus 4 is 14.

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:02.530
14 divided by 2 is 7.

00:10:02.530 --> 00:10:04.887
I have seven ravioli
and I'm gonna start by

00:10:04.887 --> 00:10:09.650
brushing some water along
the edges of the round.

00:10:09.650 --> 00:10:11.430
Okay, so I just rewatched the video.

00:10:11.430 --> 00:10:12.370
I messed up.

00:10:12.370 --> 00:10:15.130
She makes it like regular ravioli.

00:10:15.130 --> 00:10:17.230
However, I cut them all out first

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.380
because I'm really good at directions.

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:22.310
But that's okay because I was
able to do the calculations

00:10:22.310 --> 00:10:25.800
to get the right amount
of lemon plus the wedges

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:27.650
so we reduce food scraps.

00:10:27.650 --> 00:10:30.413
I am just using a lemon
whipped Burrata here.

00:10:30.413 --> 00:10:33.810
This is the same one
that @saltyseattle uses.

00:10:33.810 --> 00:10:35.080
All right!

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:36.400
Let's press them down.

00:10:36.400 --> 00:10:39.990
I've already put water on them
and just squeeze the outside.

00:10:39.990 --> 00:10:41.540
Oh God.

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:42.450
(Jasmine panting)

00:10:42.450 --> 00:10:43.670
My second one looks great!

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:46.130
Okay, so I'm putting in
the center and I'm pressing

00:10:46.130 --> 00:10:49.810
from the filling outwards so
that there are no air bubbles.

00:10:49.810 --> 00:10:52.700
I would say if you're scared of error,

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:54.230
to reduce that margin of error,

00:10:54.230 --> 00:10:56.210
to just use less filling.

00:10:56.210 --> 00:10:58.260
But then you have less filling.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.540
Choose your character!

00:10:59.540 --> 00:11:01.240
I choose flavor.

00:11:01.240 --> 00:11:02.460
So now we're gonna make the segments

00:11:02.460 --> 00:11:04.200
of the lemon using our white dough.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.240
I'm just gonna cut thin white strips

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:08.460
and I'm just gonna keep doing
this until I have plenty.

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:09.970
Brush it with some water.

00:11:09.970 --> 00:11:14.200
Okay, so now we're gonna
do eight total segments.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.380
I wanna make sure it's
pressed down all the way.

00:11:16.380 --> 00:11:17.213
Great!

00:11:17.213 --> 00:11:18.270
Okay, that looks pretty good.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:19.752
I'm just gonna keep doing this until all

00:11:19.752 --> 00:11:21.710
of them have their segments.

00:11:21.710 --> 00:11:22.804
Be right back.

00:11:22.804 --> 00:11:23.637
This is gonna take a while.

00:11:23.637 --> 00:11:25.570
Now we have gotten all our wedges.

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:27.300
It's time to make the pith.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:30.110
The pith is the white part of the lemon.

00:11:30.110 --> 00:11:32.110
Very bitter so when
you're zesting your lemon,

00:11:32.110 --> 00:11:33.700
you never wanna zest the pith.

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:36.310
Okay, now I'm gonna do the rest as wedges.

00:11:36.310 --> 00:11:37.170
Yes.

00:11:37.170 --> 00:11:38.330
Yes!

00:11:38.330 --> 00:11:40.230
This is winning, people.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:42.890
I have all my circles cut out
and to make the pith I have

00:11:42.890 --> 00:11:44.550
to use this smaller cookie cutter,

00:11:44.550 --> 00:11:48.520
place it in the center,
and cut out the middle.

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.983
Okay.

00:11:49.983 --> 00:11:51.514
Wow.

00:11:51.514 --> 00:11:54.510
I'm just hoping it'll look cuter later.

00:11:54.510 --> 00:11:56.280
So I'm gonna continue doing this

00:11:56.280 --> 00:11:58.983
and I'll be back for the rind.

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:02.470
So we got a problem.

00:12:02.470 --> 00:12:04.500
I have the wrong size cookie cutters

00:12:04.500 --> 00:12:08.510
and the size I have would
overlap the pith entirely.

00:12:08.510 --> 00:12:10.440
However, if I use one that's too big,

00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:13.140
there's nothing to glue on to it.

00:12:13.140 --> 00:12:15.220
So it would just be hanging out like that.

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:16.420
That is a no go,

00:12:16.420 --> 00:12:19.060
so what we're gonna do
is use the same size

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:21.970
but we're gonna wet it with our water glue

00:12:21.970 --> 00:12:25.293
and then just kind of situate
it in a place that works best.

00:12:26.406 --> 00:12:28.320
I have an idea!

00:12:28.320 --> 00:12:29.690
I have an idea.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:30.890
I'm gonna roll them out!

00:12:31.870 --> 00:12:32.703
Yeah!

00:12:34.120 --> 00:12:36.209
Can we get a clap sound effect here?

00:12:36.209 --> 00:12:37.786
(crowd clapping)

00:12:37.786 --> 00:12:39.000
Oh my gosh.

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:40.525
We freakin' did it.

00:12:40.525 --> 00:12:42.090
I'm so happy!

00:12:42.090 --> 00:12:43.360
Yay.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:44.580
Orange.

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:45.413
I'm so proud of this.

00:12:45.413 --> 00:12:46.810
Mimo, Mimo, come here.

00:12:46.810 --> 00:12:48.240
- Oh my gosh, you did it.

00:12:48.240 --> 00:12:49.175
- Isn't this so cute!

00:12:49.175 --> 00:12:50.008
- So cute.

00:12:50.008 --> 00:12:51.150
(both cheering)

00:12:51.150 --> 00:12:52.820
- Yes! Bye, Mimo.

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:54.282
She's going to sleep now.

00:12:54.282 --> 00:12:56.983
I'm gonna keep doing this
and I will be right back.

00:12:56.983 --> 00:12:59.110
It's the evening now, in
case you're wondering.

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:00.780
I've been waiting for this moment

00:13:00.780 --> 00:13:02.730
to cut off these little diggly poppers

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:05.930
that are poppin' out of the orange now.

00:13:05.930 --> 00:13:08.070
Okay, I'm gonna start with the wedges.

00:13:08.070 --> 00:13:09.550
These have been taking so long

00:13:09.550 --> 00:13:11.020
that when I just pressed down on it,

00:13:11.020 --> 00:13:11.910
it crunched.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:13.510
Oh, they're coming apart.

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:15.930
We're gonna finish these up
and then we'll get to boiling.

00:13:15.930 --> 00:13:18.520
I think I'm losing my mind a little bit.

00:13:18.520 --> 00:13:22.800
The TikToks are like so
short and it took me all day!

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:24.120
I can't believe we're at this point

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:25.230
but we are gonna cook it.

00:13:25.230 --> 00:13:28.510
Salting my water first and
my water has come to a boil.

00:13:28.510 --> 00:13:30.530
Now I'm just gonna gently
place them in with my hands.

00:13:30.530 --> 00:13:32.860
I'm gonna scoop it out with a spoon,

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.780
drain it on my spider.

00:13:34.780 --> 00:13:35.613
Yes!

00:13:35.613 --> 00:13:37.030
Everything stayed together!

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:38.670
I am very impressed.

00:13:38.670 --> 00:13:41.113
I'm also quite tired,
but I'm very impressed.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:43.140
Now that our ravioli's done,

00:13:43.140 --> 00:13:45.633
we're gonna toss in
this garlic cream sauce.

00:13:49.910 --> 00:13:53.780
Gonna top it with some
peas, some Pecorino cheese.

00:13:53.780 --> 00:13:55.630
Ooh, that looks good.

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:58.773
Some salt and some lemon zest.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:00.710
And here we have it.

00:14:00.710 --> 00:14:02.970
Lemon ravioli.

00:14:02.970 --> 00:14:05.930
I would charge $300 for this.

00:14:05.930 --> 00:14:06.860
More maybe.

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:09.770
This is like my midnight
snack, but I'm really excited.

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:11.580
A lot of TLC went into this.

00:14:11.580 --> 00:14:12.580
Let's give it a try.

00:14:13.556 --> 00:14:14.650
Mm.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.110
I'm very happy now.

00:14:16.110 --> 00:14:17.820
It was all worth it in the end.

00:14:17.820 --> 00:14:20.370
So lemony, so garlicky, so creamy.

00:14:20.370 --> 00:14:21.440
Was it worth it?

00:14:21.440 --> 00:14:24.080
Honestly, yes, it was worth
it because I got to make it.

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:26.220
I have a finished beautiful product.

00:14:26.220 --> 00:14:28.270
Things went a little off course.

00:14:28.270 --> 00:14:29.820
However, look at it.

00:14:29.820 --> 00:14:30.653
Gorgeous.

00:14:30.653 --> 00:14:32.430
If you guys end up making
any of these pasta shapes,

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:33.390
make sure to snap a picture,

00:14:33.390 --> 00:14:34.510
tag me on Instagram,

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:35.740
because I wanna see it.

00:14:35.740 --> 00:14:36.573
Thanks, guys.

00:14:36.573 --> 00:14:37.530
Bye.

00:14:37.530 --> 00:14:39.125
Oh, yes.

00:14:39.125 --> 00:14:40.270
(Jasmine laughing)

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:41.890
Let's go to title card.

00:14:41.890 --> 00:14:43.014
- [Man] Oh, yes!

00:14:43.014 --> 00:14:45.931
(slow funky music)

